<!--
A wrapped prize.

  The gift metaphor is the one the old ic_gift glyph established and the
  Prizes page still uses, so nothing has to be re-learned.

  White line work, at the two weights the app uses everywhere else: full for
  the shape, a little over half for secondary detail.

  It was lime — Palette.Accent — which was one step too far in the same
  direction that put the accent on the countdown figure. The accent is the
  app's action colour: it belongs on a scanned checkpoint and a filled
  progress bar, on things that mean something has happened. A drawing on a
  tile has not happened, and three lime drawings on one screen made a page of
  white type look like it was decorated rather than laid out.

  The two earlier versions are worth remembering: filled shapes in three
  palette colours read as clip-art dropped on the screen, because solid colour
  carries far more weight than the frosted glass around it. An outline weighs
  what an icon weighs, and white is what the icons are.
-->
